{
  "id": "language.frozen_addresses",
  "type": "custom",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "description": "Closed-set vocabulary with deterministically-pinned base-60 addresses. Every ENKI installation worldwide assigns identical addresses to these tokens so cross-ENKI dictionaries can be merged by simple address-equality, not name-matching. Subtype indexes within `form`: noun=0, verb=1, adjective=2, function_word=3, initialism=4, number_word=5, name_token=6, unknown=7, lemma=8. Address format: 11.<subtype_idx>.<sequence>. Sequences within each subtype are assigned in the order tokens appear in this file — order is therefore part of the public contract; never reorder existing entries.",
  "rationale": "Closed-set vocabulary (function words, common numbers, name particles) does not vary corpus-to-corpus. By pinning their addresses globally, distributed ENKI installations can merge their language_form_distributions by SQL union rather than name-reconciliation. New tokens append; existing entries are immutable.",
